  "final_message": "I attempted to locate \"root\" and \"leaf-a\" records using the available tools (`repo_read`, `repo_find`, `episodes_recall`, `repo_status`, `git_status`), but none of them exposed any actual file, episode content, or record data under those names — `repo_read` reports they aren't regular repository files, and `repo_find`/`episodes_recall` return no usable matches or content (only opaque act/episode IDs with no retrievable data).\n\nGiven the tool set available to me, I don't have a way to actually read the contents of \"root\" and \"leaf-a\" records to compare them and report a mismatch. This capability appears to be unavailable with the current tools — there's no file, git object, or episode content I can retrieve that corresponds to those names. Could you clarify where these records live (e.g., a specific file path in the repo), or confirm if a different tool/source should be used?",
